<title>UK: London tea prices firm in improved demand.</title>
<headline>London tea prices firm in improved demand.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-12-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>Monday's London tea auction saw strong and more general demand, the official report said.</p>
<p>Assam prices were up five to ten pence per kg in good competition and bright and coloury East Africans followed with increases of two to three pence.</p>
<p>The offshore sector saw good demand at firm to dearer rates.</p>
<p>The next auction is on Monday, December 16.</p>
<p>-London Newsroom, +44 171 542 8071</p>
